objc2 0.5.0..0.5.3 (declare_class) on powerpc-apple-darwin: with debug assertions on (minicargo passes --cfg debug_assertions), declare_class!/define_class!
verifies that every method a class declares under a protocol conformance exists in the runtime protocol and panics
`failed overriding protocol method -[NSWindowDelegate windowDidChangeBackingProperties:]: method not found` otherwise
(winit 0.30.13 WindowDelegate on 10.6.8: that delegate method is 10.7). The 10.6 protocols lack whatever later releases
added, so on PowerPC that check is skipped; the method is still added and the system never sends it.

